{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:92376",
  "title": "Important: nodejs:24 security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-30 00:01:28"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-30 00:14:19"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* ip-address: ip-address: Denial of Service via unbounded IPv6 address parsing (CVE-2026-101911)\n\n* brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via uncontrolled recursion in nested brace patterns (CVE-2026-102278)\n\n* brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via crafted brace patterns (CVE-2026-102277)\n\n* brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via stack exhaustion from crafted brace patterns (CVE-2026-102276)\n\n* brotli: Out-of-Bounds Write in Google Brotli Decoder (CVE-2026-111497)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: TLS certificate hostname bypass via fullwidth-digit IP hostnames (CVE-2026-105483)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: TLS certificate hostname bypass via non-canonical IP hostnames (CVE-2026-106069)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: dns.resolve truncates hostnames containing a NUL character (CVE-2026-105482)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: predictable random values via snapshot entropy cache reuse (CVE-2026-106074)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: Permission model bypass via wildcard path matching flaw (CVE-2026-106071)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: Response desynchronization via improper HTTP keep-alive connection reuse (CVE-2026-105481)\n\n* nodejs: Node.js: Filesystem read permission bypass via fs.realpathSync() (CVE-2026-106073)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: Authentication bypass via non-canonical IPv4 hostname verification (CVE-2026-106072)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* nodejs:24/nodejs: Rebase to the latest Node.js 24 release [rhel-8] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-289763)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
